WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:10.118
In tutorial 7.2, you'll read
your search and traffic,

00:00:10.168 --> 00:00:12.972
and see which searches and
pages bring you visitors.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:19.158
First, open Search & traffic. The top
shows your clicks, your impressions,

00:00:19.208 --> 00:00:21.033
the times you showed up in search,

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:24.718
your click-through rate and average
position over the last four weeks.

00:00:25.697 --> 00:00:29.047
Click-through rate is the share of
people who saw your site in search,

00:00:29.097 --> 00:00:29.974
and clicked it.

00:00:32.251 --> 00:00:35.906
Next, the week in brief sums
up your week in plain words.

00:00:35.956 --> 00:00:39.631
Below it, Google Analytics shows
the visits search brought you,

00:00:39.681 --> 00:00:41.312
and what those visitors did.

00:00:42.286 --> 00:00:46.111
Then two daily charts compare the
last four weeks with the four before,

00:00:46.161 --> 00:00:47.733
with your new pages marked.

00:00:49.761 --> 00:00:53.886
Did your changes help? follows
every page you published or changed,

00:00:53.936 --> 00:00:57.668
and gives a verdict, like Likely
helped, once there's enough data.

00:00:59.261 --> 00:01:02.486
Traffic by channel shows
how people reach your site,

00:01:02.536 --> 00:01:07.143
and Organic landing pages shows the
pages visitors from search arrive on.

00:01:08.311 --> 00:01:11.366
Now, Queries lists every
search you appear in.

00:01:11.416 --> 00:01:14.991
Click Striking distance to see the
searches where you're close to the top,

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:21.429
the ones worth improving first. You can
also filter by Top 10, New, Lost or Tracked.

00:01:22.422 --> 00:01:25.647
Then What changed this week
shows your winners and losers,

00:01:25.697 --> 00:01:29.697
and New and Lost show searches
that appeared or dropped away.

00:01:29.747 --> 00:01:32.946
Click Losers to see the searches
that lost the most clicks.

00:01:33.971 --> 00:01:39.071
Finally, Google Trends shows whether interest
in your keywords is rising or stable,

00:01:39.121 --> 00:01:41.275
and the related searches people use.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:47.750
And Weekly history shows a whole year of
your weekly numbers, with every new page,

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.719
audit and search update marked.

00:01:50.971 --> 00:01:55.121
So you see which searches and pages
bring visitors, what changed this week,

00:01:55.171 --> 00:01:56.525
and where to work next.

00:01:57.975 --> 00:02:02.125
So, read the headline numbers and the
week in brief, check your changes,

00:02:02.175 --> 00:02:06.511
channels and pages, find your best
searches, and check Google Trends.

00:02:07.531 --> 00:02:10.456
Now you know your search
and traffic. Next,

00:02:10.506 --> 00:02:13.763
track where your keywords
rank in tutorial 7.3.
